sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor UserA as "User A"
    actor UserB as "User B"
    participant BrowserA as "User A Browser"
    participant BrowserB as "User B Browser"
    participant API as "ASP.NET Core API"
    participant Prefs as "Preference Endpoints"
    participant Repo as "Repository Endpoints"
    participant Worker as "Background Analyzer"
    participant Storage as "Azure Table Storage"
    participant GitHub as "GitHub + Local Repo Cache"
    participant Failures as "Failed Operation Queue"

    UserA->>BrowserA: Open repositories page
    UserB->>BrowserB: Open repositories page
    BrowserA->>API: GET /api/repositories
    BrowserB->>API: GET /api/repositories
    API->>Storage: Read repositories by UserId partition
    Storage-->>API: User-scoped repository list
    API-->>BrowserA: Repository list
    API-->>BrowserB: Repository list

    par "Independent preference changes"
        UserA->>BrowserA: Save chart mode + file extensions
        BrowserA->>Prefs: PUT /api/settings/user-preferences
        Prefs->>Storage: Upsert preferences for User A
        Storage-->>Prefs: Preferences saved
        Prefs-->>BrowserA: 200 OK
    and
        UserB->>BrowserB: Save chart mode + file extensions
        BrowserB->>Prefs: PUT /api/settings/user-preferences
        Prefs->>Storage: Upsert preferences for User B
        Storage-->>Prefs: Preferences saved
        Prefs-->>BrowserB: 200 OK
    end

    par "Concurrent analysis requests"
        UserA->>BrowserA: Re-analyze repository
        BrowserA->>Repo: POST /api/repositories/{id}/reanalyze
        Repo-->>BrowserA: 202 Accepted
        Repo->>Worker: Queue user-scoped re-analysis
    and
        UserB->>BrowserB: Analyze repository
        BrowserB->>Repo: POST /api/repositories/{id}/analyses?force=false
        Repo-->>BrowserB: 202 Accepted
        Repo->>Worker: Queue user-scoped analysis
    end

    Worker->>GitHub: Clone or pull target repository
    GitHub-->>Worker: Repository snapshot
    Worker->>Storage: Write repository, commit, top-file, and failure-safe metrics
    alt "Processing error occurs"
        Worker->>Failures: Record failed operation context
        Failures->>Storage: Persist retry metadata
    else "Processing succeeds"
        Storage-->>Worker: Derived metrics committed
    end

    Note over API,Storage: Conflict boundary is the authenticated UserId partition.\nCross-user writes are blocked by ownership checks.
    Note over Worker,Storage: For repeated requests on the same repository, writes are idempotent at repository scope and the latest successful derivation becomes the visible state.
    Note over BrowserA,BrowserB: The client uses request-response refresh and polling; there is no real-time push channel in the current architecture.